PixelCanvasEffect_083126
Last reviewed: 083126

Originating Prompt: we are trying to integrate functionality similar to the
app , desktop terminal effect in python on github. he is doing something
about rendering each character space like a pixel space and its really
cool. id like to have some functionality like that in deskapp

Interpretation: The user has seen a GitHub project that renders terminal
output by treating every character cell as an addressable "pixel"
(mapping a numeric intensity or color value per cell to a glyph/color
pair), used to build animated full-screen terminal effects. DeskApp
already has a partial example of this pattern in deskapp/mods/fire.py
(the Flames class keeps a flat intensity buffer `b` and a `gameboard`
grid, then maps intensity to a glyph ramp each frame). The user wants
this "pixel space" idea generalized into reusable DeskApp functionality
rather than reimplemented ad hoc per module, so future effects (fire,
plasma, matrix rain, image-to-ascii, etc.) can be built on a shared
abstraction. The exact source project was not linked; a link would let
us confirm the actual rendering technique (character ramp only, vs.
character + 24-bit/256-color per cell, vs. half-block "upper pixel"
tricks) instead of assuming it matches fire.py's approach.

Promoted from .github/proposals/TODO_PixelCanvasEffect_083126.prop on
083126 at the user's request ("please go ahead with adding a proposal
document... then we can review what you have").

Proposal:

- [ ] Confirm/refine scope with the user, ideally after they share a link
      to the reference project, to settle whether per-cell color is
      in scope for v1 or a later iteration
- [ ] Add a PixelCanvas class (new file, likely
      deskapp/src/pixel_canvas.py, exported from deskapp/__init__.py
      alongside existing core exports such as widgets) that owns:
    - [ ] a width/height grid of numeric cell values (0-9 or 0-255
          intensity scale)
    - [ ] a configurable character ramp (list of glyphs, dark to
          bright, generalized from Flames.chars / og_chars)
    - [ ] an optional per-cell color/attr mapping hook, kept separate
          from glyph selection so callers can opt in or skip it
    - [ ] a Render(Mod, Panel, Row, Col, Height, Width) method that
          writes the grid to the DeskApp backend via Module.write(),
          matching the calling convention used by
          deskapp/src/widgets.py's ScrollList/ResultGrid
- [ ] Refactor deskapp/mods/fire.py's Flames class to build its buffer
      on top of PixelCanvas instead of maintaining its own
      buffer/gameboard/char-mapping logic, proving the abstraction
      works for an existing effect without changing fire.py's visible
      behavior
- [ ] Add one new example effect module built on PixelCanvas (e.g. a
      "plasma" or "matrix rain" mod under deskapp/mods/) to demonstrate
      reuse beyond fire and give a second concrete reference point
- [ ] Add a standalone examples/ex_pixel_canvas.py demonstrating
      PixelCanvas usage outside of a full mod, consistent with existing
      examples/ex_*.py conventions
- [ ] Update README.md's Core API section only if PixelCanvas is
      exported as a top-level deskapp symbol (mirrors how CoreWidgets
      were documented under Proposal 09)
- [ ] No changes to deskapp/mods/apt.py, about.py, buttons.py,
      hunter.py, memory_viewer.py, or unrelated core modules
- [ ] Roll version to 0.10.0 and update .github/changelog.ai on
      completion, crediting Proposal 10

